    <statement><p>Let <m>P</m> be the plane in space that intersects the <m>x</m>-axis at <m>-1</m>,
the <m>y</m>-axis at <m>4</m>, and the <m>z</m>-axis at <m>5</m>.  Find a vector
<m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;v\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m> that is perpendicular to <m>P</m>.</p>
<p><m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;v\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m> = <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <hint><B>Hint: </B>If you can find a vector perpendicular to<em>two</em> vectors in the plane, it will be perpendicular to all of them.  Can you find two vector in this plane?
</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;20,-5,-4\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
